p.src:
Write the field schematically as $\Phi(x)
=
\frac{v+h(x)}{\sqrt{2}}
\exp\!\left(
  \frac{i\theta(x)}{v}
\right).$ The variable $\theta$ describes motion along the trough. The variable $h$ changes the radius. In a gauge theory the appropriate angular degrees of freedom become the longitudinal components of the massive weak bosons, while $h$ remains as a propagating scalar particle: the Higgs boson.

